    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW27tU7SZxGevT2nhsMSrwUfi)_\n\n- The README section \"Reviewing and merging AI-made changes on macOS\" now lives in `emacs-modular/.config/emacs-modular/docs/architecture/macos-review-and-merge.org` (where the other architecture notes are). The README keeps a two-line summary and a link.\n- Updated for Stow: no yadm, `~/dotfiles` is the only clone (SourceGit uses it, not `~/src/dotfiles-test`), and Magit relies on `vc-follow-symlinks`.\n- Rewritten as bullet lists; ADR links adjusted to the new depth.\n- Fixed two dead README links (they pointed at `.config/emacs-modular/...` and a `docs/main.org` that does not exist).\n- `adr/README.org` now links to the new file instead of the README anchor.\n\nDocs only, no CHANGELOG edits. Links were checked by path, not opened in Emacs.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCussRz2J4gUL1kqwC)_",
